---
description: Defense picks, weekly website updates, source snapshots, and accuracy reports
alwaysApply: true
---

For defense picks or updates to andrewbernal.com:
- Use the existing sibling Andrew-Bernal-Website Astro/Cloudflare project and
  follow Fantasy-Football-Tool/docs/DEFENSE-PUBLISHING.md. Resolve minor domain
  typos from this context; do not create another website or change hosting.
- An explicit publish/upload request authorizes the normal tested Git deployment.
  Complete it and verify live pages; do not stop at a plan or local files.
- Use the requested season/week explicitly. An update is a bounded publication
  task, not a request to invent a model, run broad research, install plugins,
  create recurring jobs, or change the user's fantasy roster.
- Rank by opponent implied total, ascending (finding 27). Never use ESPN fantasy
  projections or nfelo model spreads as bookmaker lines. Exact ties share rank;
  alphabetical order is display only. Small gaps are weak preferences.
- Reuse a saved US Odds API snapshot under 24 hours old, or fetch one explicitly
  with the existing market tool (2 credits). Pair spread/total within each book,
  then median opponent points. Keep source time, bookmaker inputs and quota.
  Do not query per defense or per page view; do not print/publish the API key.
- Verify full requested-week coverage and pregame status. Missing future lines
  remain pending, never guessed or labeled as byes. Do not claim a two-week hold
  without both weeks' inputs. Keep personal availability advice off public pages.
- Preserve published editions byte-for-byte. Publish revisions at a new dated
  edition URL; retain original week routes and link the current edition correctly.
- Grade Week 1 from its September 6 original, not a later snapshot. Include all
  picks and misses, custom scoring, pending games, zero/negative points, and the
  denominator. Correlation is not percent accuracy; one week is not validation.
- Use concise public prose: current picks, source/date, calculation, limitations,
  and links to methodology/accuracy. Avoid internal implementation commentary.
- Run relevant tests/build, inspect desktop/mobile pages, deploy reviewed files
  only, and verify the live edition/data and accuracy URLs before saying live.
